            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Then sorry, no, this is out of scope for 'mini.ai' for at least these reasons:\r\n- I would like to adhere to built-in neovim definition of dot-repeat that it \"repeats last change\". As selection is not a change, then it should not work with dot repeat.\r\n- Making it work with any other special key to repeat would introduce some non-trivial cache handling (on top existing non-trivial one).\r\n- To somewhat remedy the need to type `inf` many times, it supports `v:count`, so `2inf` will work as if `infinf`.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
