        },
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Support for dot-repeat means that if user does an edit using 'mini.ai' textobject (like `dif`; delete inside function call), it can be dot-repeated with textobject being recomputed at the new cursor position.\r\n\r\nDot-repeating visual selection is out of scope. See [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/521#issuecomment-1764618764) for more details.",
            "created_at": "2024-07-23T04:33:32Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/521#issuecomment-2244232512",
            "id": 2244232512,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/521",
